/*
 * Implements validation for `unsafe` expressions in Ymir.
 *
 * An `unsafe` block temporarily enables operations that bypass the language’s
 * safety guarantees(raw memory access, unchecked casts, pointer arithmetic,
 * etc.). Ymir enforces that unsafe contexts:
 *
 *   - cannot be nested
 *   - must be explicitly delimited
 *   - restore the previous safety state even if validation fails
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::value::control::unsafe_
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/value/control/unsafe_.yr
